From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:52:24 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: Apply the init quirks again after a resume
 that reset the amp

Amps outside an SDZ group drop SDZ across system sleep, so they come
back from a power-on reset. The resume's regcache_sync() restores the
cached registers, but the init quirks applied at probe also write TI's
quirk page (0xfd), which is volatile: the reset clears those writes and
nothing writes them again. The amp then runs without them for the rest
of the boot.

On a J316 (M1 Pro) that latched an over-current on a woofer amp at the
first stream after a resume, one cycle in a few:

  tas2764 3-003c: fault: over current
  tas2764 3-003c: other context to the fault: 02,19,00,00,00

even with every speaker PCM closed across the sleep, and the speaker
protection supervisor then kept the speakers withdrawn.

Apply the init quirks again after the cache sync for an SN012776 whose
SDZ went low, as the probe does. Members of an SDZ group keep SDZ high
across sleep and their registers with it, so they are left alone.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 2046f353881cd9ada7458ace25fb70f8447fb6d8)
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 2bb4641979..52c8694272 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -326,6 +326,7 @@ static int tas2764_update_pwr_ctrl(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764)
 }
 
 static void tas2764_flush_shutdown(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764);
+static int tas2764_apply_init_quirks(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
 /*
@@ -402,6 +403,16 @@ static int tas2764_codec_resume(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	regcache_cache_only(tas2764->regmap, false);
 
 	ret = regcache_sync(tas2764->regmap);
+	/*
+	 * An amp whose SDZ went low came back from a power-on reset, and the
+	 * cache sync restores only the cached registers: the init quirks
+	 * also write TI's volatile quirk page, which the reset cleared and
+	 * nothing wrote again. Without them a J316 woofer amp latched an
+	 * over-current at the first stream after a resume. Apply them again,
+	 * as the probe does.
+	 */
+	if (ret >= 0 && !tas2764->sdz_group && tas2764->devid == DEVID_SN012776)
+		ret = tas2764_apply_init_quirks(tas2764);
 	if (ret >= 0)
 		ret = tas2764_update_pwr_ctrl(tas2764);
 
